  "answer": "In May 2026, the Import/OCR category comprised **112 support tickets**, the largest ticket category (27.2% of total volume) [NL-029#NL-029-S02][NL-012#NL-012-S07].\n\n**Documented root causes:** The majority of these tickets relate to image-only or poorly scanned PDF documents that fail to process or result in garbled text output in KnowledgeHub; clients upload historical documents, safety manuals, or legacy compliance guides that lack native text layers, causing indexing workers to generate empty document indexes [NL-029#NL-029-S02]. The ingestion pipeline relies on standard PDF text extraction, so image-only PDFs fail to extract text, leading to empty document models or TutorChat being unable to generate citations [NL-029#NL-029-S05].\n\n**Recommended operational response:** The Support Operations department recommends developing a **Pre-Ingestion Scanning Tool** — a diagnostic utility in the KnowledgeHub admin dashboard that analyzes uploaded PDFs for text layers and warns users if a file is image-only before it enters the ingestion queue, proactively reducing Import/OCR tickets [NL-029#NL-029-S06]. In the interim, support agents advise customers to run external OCR tools before uploading files, with a permanent resolution requiring the release of the Advanced OCR Pipeline planned for August 2026 [NL-029#NL-029-S05].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
